<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<topic id="0de6046f-c5e3-4dc8-abd8-1b9a8d7d68c7" revisionNumber="1">
  <developerConceptualDocument
    xmlns="http://ddue.schemas.microsoft.com/authoring/2003/5"
    xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink">

    <introduction>
				<para>
					When deploying your application, you must make sure the DemiCode.Scheduling assembly
					is available from your assembly.
				</para>
				<para>
					The DemiCode.Scheduling assembly should automatically be copied to the project
					output directory when you compile your application, and can be deployed by beeing
					copied with the calling assembly.
				</para>
				<para>
					<legacyBold>Note:</legacyBold> If you have installed the DemiCode.Scheduling assembly in the GAC
					on your development workstation or build server, this may not happen and you need
					to make the assembly available to your project's output. This can be done in one
					of the follwing ways:
				</para>
				<list class="bullet">
					<listItem>By setting the Copy Local property setting for the DemiCode.Scheduling reference
						to true.</listItem>
					<listItem>By manually copying the assembly (DemiCode.Scheduling.dll) to the applications'
						executable file's directory. </listItem>
					<listItem>By installing it in the global assembly cache (GAC) on the target computer. (See
						also <externalLink>
	<linkText>How to: Install Assemblies in the Global Assembly Cache</linkText>
	<linkUri>ms-help://MS.VSCC.v80/MS.MSDN.v80/MS.VisualStudio.v80.en/dv_fxnetcf/html/5aa081e4-13b3-4646-a391-9c184394ac62.htm</linkUri>
	</externalLink>.) </listItem>
				</list>
    </introduction>


	

    <relatedTopics>
    </relatedTopics>

  </developerConceptualDocument>
</topic>
